{"body":"Worker 1's full-shard evidence at `1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5` assigns `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-1` through `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-12` to #1159 in `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/final-188-scientific-review-v1.json`. Its active shard report repeats that attribution. The live #1159 body covers only the three earlier canary findings (`IR-DRAFT-1`, `IR-DRAFT-2`, `IR-VALIDATION-1`) and has no comments expanding its scope.\n\nThis issue records the distinct full-shard finding set and the publication provenance correction `W01-PUBLISHED-001`. Preserve #1159's canary identity. The full-shard review reports these corrections in isolated proposals, independently re-reviewed before publication:\n\n| Finding | Defect and corrected scope |\n| --- | --- |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-1 | Distinguish the unsuccessful JCM956 retrieval from the explicit JCM574 fallback and actual MDS context. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-2 | Remove the false discrepancy between frozen `10 MILLIMOLAR` and `10 mM` for case105; retain the actual reagent-form uncertainty. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-3 | Correct named case104's receiving dose from 1 to 2 mL. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-4 | Distinguish case138's current recipe1188 direct reference to852 from the frozen1187 inheritance narrative. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-5 | Correct case103's receiving dose from 5 to10 mL. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-6 | Correct case112's receiving dose from 1 to1.5 mL. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-7 | Remove root40's unsupported aqueous assertion; retain the actual solvent evidence gap. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-8 | Keep Middlebrook7H10 dry base distinct from the NCIT enriched finished medium. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-9 | Retire source-local/generic aliases that would resolve globally, including bare numbered pointers; qualify the JCM431 stock name and mapping label. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-10 | Reconcile four duplicate proposal families while preserving each source-case/occurrence lineage. The NBRC1257/1321 bicarbonate and sulfide pairs are also tracked by #1166; NBRC1339 phenanthrene and NBRC943 Metal44 are the other two families. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-11 | Preserve added-water quantities without treating them as final solution volumes or inferred final concentrations; retain explicit preparation and comparison bases. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-12 | Correct false or unrelated missing-evidence requirements for cases38/64 and34/59/66, preserving the source-supported remaining gaps. |\n\nThe separate coordinator findings remain on #1163, #1164, #1166, #1167 and #1168. This tracker does not replace them or grant maintained-record, mapping, role, component or release approval.\n\nAppend an immutable provenance correction or successor, update active report/issue references and the PR description, and preserve old primary captures, proposal payloads, native saved reviews and canary files byte-for-byte. Do not rewrite the historical review merely to conceal its mistaken issue reference. The published correction must bind the exact prior review hash and all twelve finding IDs. Obtain independent final-head re-review of the new references and confirm the scientific payloads are unchanged.\n\nIndependent evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w01-published-head-review-v1/finding-001-tracker-scope.json`; prior full-shard review SHA256 `02b2be72b448d35b573ad992a3d2c98afcd3f16430709e10d6837564b595edcf`; active report SHA256 `762ba8d961cfdfc856c724d2a4b232cc776bbc43861e34a0f7d28af70b06f1df`. A live all-state GitHub issue search for `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT` found no existing dedicated tracker. The local evidence search included ignored files. No scientific payload defect was found in the independent 188-case/76-proposal reassessment.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkGfv9A","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"This comment supplies the correction and re-review provenance for the full-shard findings already listed in this issue. It also records the continuation publication findings here before the pending CultureMech comment correction. Issue [#1159](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1159) retains only the three original canary findings.\n\n**W01-PUBLISHED-001 — tracker scope.** The historical [full 188-case scientific review](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/final-188-scientific-review-v1.json) at `1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5` has SHA256 `02b2be72b448d35b573ad992a3d2c98afcd3f16430709e10d6837564b595edcf`. Its scientific conclusions remain unchanged, but its assignment of the continuation findings to #1159 is superseded by this tracker. The exact affected IDs are:\n\n`IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-1`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-2`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-3`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-4`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-5`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-6`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-7`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-8`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-9`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-10`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-11`, `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-12`.\n\nThe existing issue table describes the defects. Their independently reviewed corrections are supported by these immutable receipts:\n\n- Findings 1 and 2: [JCM 956 retrieval classification and fallback](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/artifact-finding-rereview-v1.json); [the corrected 10 mM unit comparison](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/artifact-finding-rereview-v2.json).\n- Findings 3–6: [receiving-dose and frozen/current-provenance corrections](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/named-stocks-corrections-rereview-v1.json).\n- Findings 7–12: the [final scientific review](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/final-188-scientific-review-v1.json) records each correction and independent disposition, with [exact case/proposal coverage](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/final-review-coverage-v1.json) and the separate [five-case requirement rereview for finding 12](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/artifact-finding-v12-rereview-v1.json). This includes the dry-base identity, source-local alias resolution, duplicate stocks and literal preparation quantities. The review covers 188 source-case outcomes and 76 isolated proposals with retained source and owner limits; it does not approve maintained integration or release.\n\n**Publication findings 1 and 2.** `IR-PUB-ARTIFACT-1` inserted spaces inside seven exact proposal IDs; `IR-PUB-ARTIFACT-2` inferred 0.4 mg/L from the JCM 1462 listing of 0.4 mg plus 1 L added water. Both were corrected before posting. The [original publication review](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/publication-artifact-review-v1.json) and [independent publication rereview](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/publication-artifact-rereview-v2.json) bind those corrections. Earlier review approval is superseded only for the newly identified case 24 classification below.\n\n**IR-PUB-ARTIFACT-3 (IR-PUB-3) — published case 24 grouping.** The [CultureMech #408 comment](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/issues/408#issuecomment-6717638312) includes zero-based case 24, EZMix-N-Z-amine A, in the volume-to-mass group. The [complete TOGO M2816 source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/root_substances/captures/primary/b98772426e9db9e378a4.json) gives value `0.1` with unit `(w/v)`, whereas the [frozen CultureMech:009364 occurrence](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/root_substances/captures/case-024.json) at `ingredients/5` gives `0.1 G_PER_L`. This establishes a historical percentage/denominator clarification, not a demonstrated volume-to-mass substitution. The likely original article full text was not successfully retrieved. The scientific case decision and supported EZMix product proposal already preserve this boundary and are unchanged.\n\nThe prepared correction removes case 24 from the volume row and adds a separate source-quantity-notation row. The immutable observation is `shard/issues/publication-posting-finding-v1.json`, SHA256 `9f83ab47df199fcacef2f464928a4ce3b7d7a0fc62ec119f513cdf7e9664d98e`; independent confirmation and exact-body review are in `shard/independent_review/publication-finding-3-rereview-v1.json`, SHA256 `bae48f96d56f6e4eff3cb98548583006f39202a65b80c91ec80d47a6b5337e9a`. That review also explicitly supersedes the earlier missed publication grouping approval. Its old instruction to post the tracking comment to #1159 is superseded by the user's #1173 routing instruction. This comment records the finding here before editing the existing CultureMech comment. Completion still requires exact corrected-body readback; no published-correction completion is claimed yet.\n\nOriginal posted bodies/readbacks, primary captures, proposals, native saved reviews and canary files remain preserved. The separate coordinator findings stay on [#1163](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163), [#1164](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1164), [#1166](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166), [#1167](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167) and [#1168](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1168). Active report and metadata routing will be corrected through an immutable provenance successor and independently checked at the final head; no historical native review is rewritten.\n\n<!-- mim-review-round: all-unmatched-20261107-worker01-continuation; mim-fingerprints: W01-PUBLISHED-001,IR-PUB-ARTIFACT-1,IR-PUB-ARTIFACT-2,IR-PUB-ARTIFACT-3 -->\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T05:23:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173#issuecomment-6717698036","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkGmkPA","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Worker03 independently confirmed and corrected the same alias-boundary defect described by this issue's `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-9`. This records the precise worker03 disposition without creating a duplicate issue or selecting a cross-shard payload winner.\n\n`M-JCM431-POINTER-1`: proposal `m-jcm431_selenite_tungstate_solution` inherited `Selenite-tungstate solution see Medium No. 431` as resolving RAW_TEXT. The pointer lacks a provider namespace. JCM1081's actual hyperlink to JCM431 and MediaDive S4878's ingredient1921 context establish occurrence-specific routing and the four-component stock preparation, but they do not make a bare numbered pointer a global identity name. Under MAPPING_SEMANTICS Section3, the corrected proposal preserves the text and original `source: mim-queue` as REJECTED_LABEL and appends a curation-history event.\n\nExact worker03 proposal scope:\n\n- `CM_NAME:7af57ea537b7e7a3a0e90c926bc62a599ba905329b046dfd8f311a2ebca109ab`\n- `CM_NAME:fef0391344c383fe93459d6562a1fd9689c473ab98703b37785de5d40ca7a8df`\n- `KG_CASE:aa90b6b77f1a663fb5586f7b823e46b7037b9838ff6f881eb339966cd909872b`\n\nBefore-owner SHA256 remains `ad02ea5d31f05ad4f5a71af9718cab059c17a983d01fb0aa101d6b61b8a94549`. Corrected isolated after-payload SHA256 is `83ffd40a40010e3b5c997565750e523539ebe3bfc9bc5332d42f2f7aef16db1f`.\n\nThe initial independent materials review missed this inherited resolving alias. Its exact prior bytes (SHA256 `2625ce3c28ccf98b774e18ab27298e2902e9ea7d4c56bbb7b2bf2379c658ac99`) are retained as `chemicals/independent-review-of-materials-before-cross-shard.json`, and the earlier author payload/core are archived under `materials/superseded/jcm431-pointer-v1/`. The amended separate review, `chemicals/independent-review-of-materials.json`, SHA256 `538eaf7b66609279db6e4d6544b53d4a87a3aa469fab256bfa81dc1fcbde70af`, explicitly supersedes that approval and verifies the corrected bytes. All paths are under `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-03/`.\n\nWorker01's exact payload at head `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c`, SHA256 `5e6c9e17dba64208e589d3f872006080c2ac5b00aef2307c2c966a34f5069731`, was read and byte-verified as context. Worker03 independently assessed its own primary-source applicability and did not adopt the peer payload or its additional case set. The coordinator still must reconcile the complete proposals, component grounding and both source-case sets. #718's source/owner obligations and all native release holds remain explicit; no maintained edit, merge or export approval follows from this correction.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T05:37:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173#issuecomment-6717809724","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1173,"state":"OPEN","title":"Track Worker 1 full-shard findings separately from the canary provenance","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173"}
